[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] &gt;&gt; Hello and welcome back. Firstly, I just want to say a huge'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'thanks. [music] I genuinely wasn\'t expecting my first Leica Q video to get the response it did. I had so many positive comments from you guys and some people asked questions about how I filmed the video, what kind of settings I used. So, I thought today'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'d take you behind the scenes and show you how I filmed the video and what settings I changed in camera. So, firstly, let\'s talk about color. Quite a few of you commented on how good'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the footage looked in the standard color and film look profiles. There were a few mentions about saturation and contrast, so I thought I\'d take you through the in-camera settings and how you can adjust the image to your liking. To adjust color settings, we\'re going to'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'first head into the pro menu. Scroll down and find the adjust sub menu. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; You can choose from five levels of saturation. One, two,'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'three, four, and five. You can choose from three levels of sharpness. Low, medium,'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and high. You can choose from five levels of contrast. One, two, three, four,'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and five. It doesn\'t take much to alter the character of your image, [music] so play around, find the combination of settings that works for your project. Another question I saw was regarding the film look profiles and whether they had'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adjustable strength. For the six [music] non-Leica branded profiles, you can adjust the strength and you have three options: low, medium, and high.'

[02:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Low, medium, and high. The three Leica branded color profiles, that\'s Leica Chrome, Leica Natural, and Leica Vivid, [music] they all have fixed'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'strength. And that\'s because they\'ve been developed by Leica color experts in collaboration with Insta360 specifically [music] for the Lena Ultra. Now, you still have access to the adjust menu that gives you saturation, contrast, and sharpness. In my first'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video, all the film looks were set to medium strength. Everything in the adjust menu was also set to medium. The low angle shot. This seemed to get a lot of attention, so I\'m going to show'

[02:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you now how I created it. The first thing you\'re going to need is a selfie stick or similar. Attach that to the Lena Ultra. Then, rotate the camera 90° to put it into vertical shooting mode.'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then a further 90° to put it into inverted shooting mode. Detach the screen and extend the selfie stick so the camera is at the desired height. Position yourself in the middle of the'

[03:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'motion path you want to walk. Frame your shot and then lock the gimbal. Move to the start position of your motion path. Check the screen and hit record. And then [music] carefully do the ninja walk across the motion path.'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; You can actually have lots of fun playing around with the height of this shot, especially if you have a long selfie stick. This is genuinely one of my favorite features of the Lena Ultra.'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I also had quite a few questions about how I created the smooth sideways tracking shots. I like to call these parallax shots. Now, there are two main methods for doing this: gimbal lock and deep track. So, let\'s cut to Joe in'

[03:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the field and he\'ll show you how. &gt;&gt; So, what I do to start with, kind of like frame my shot. The good thing about this is I can just turn my gimbal and not have to worry too much.'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And I kind of like get it roughly in the center, so like the point of interest in the center of the shot. Okay, that\'s kind of a nice composition there. If I turn like this, my camera moves. So, I\'ve actually set the gimbal lock up on this custom key here. So, I\'m just'

[04:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to first of all set that. There we go. Gimbal is now locked. So, even if I turn the camera, as you can see that camera head is just locked onto that scene. Play around with the zoom. Get a shot that kind of works for you. I'

[04:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'think I\'m going to want the quality of the three times lens. Maybe like that. Okay? So, then what happens is as you pull back, when they cross, they\'ll be kind of in the middle of the frame together. So, then what I normally do'

[04:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'d start my shot here. So, like at the most extreme point, always go a bit further than you think you want to go. Going to hit record. Ninja walk. And there we go. Nice little parallax'

[04:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot. Okay, so we\'re back in the menu here and instead of using basic settings, let\'s switch by swiping across to pro. So, first thing you\'re going to want to change is your exposure to be on manual'

[05:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'exposure. So, rule of thumb and go 120, which is double. Then going to come out of there. I\'m going to bump the ISO up slightly cuz it was showing me wanted a bit more exposure. This is why we need'

[05:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'an exposure meter. So, now my exposure is not going to change. Just so you don\'t get a drifting color, change your white balance. So, we\'ve got manual exposure set, manual white balance set and now the last thing we\'re going to'

[05:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'change is the focus mode. The standard default, which is AFC, which is continuous. Great for like things like walking around, vlogging, all that kind of stuff. But actually, for things like this, you really want control over the'

[05:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'focus. So, we\'re going to change that to AFS, which is single. So, basically it\'s like a tap to focus. It will lock the focus on the object we tap on until we tap on another object after. Let\'s do exactly what we did before. We\'re going'

[05:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to line up the shot. And in fact, I\'m going to go to this position. So, as you can see there, in my shot, that is where the background point of interest has the most visibility. Like, it\'s in the sort of gap. That\'s probably going to be the'

[06:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'position where you really want to sort of center the frame when you\'re at that point in the track. Then we\'re going to tap. There we go. So, we\'ve tapped on the church. All right, now I\'m going to lock'

[06:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the gimbal. That gimbal\'s now locked again. And we have a little bit more freedom to move the camera now. And we\'re going to do exactly the same thing again. So, we\'re going to come back past the point where we want the track to start, hit'

[06:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'record, and then we\'re going to do our track. Now, I\'m holding this really low because I can\'t hold two devices up really high above my head. But obviously, like as'

[06:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can see here, it would probably benefit to have a bit more height. Um so, that those lovely parts of the church, kind of like there, are more visible. So, you could put the Insta360 Nano on a pole and then just get a'

[06:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'little bit more height out of that and take the screen off. You could achieve something like this. I\'m going to now do a slightly zoomed-in version of this. And there you go. And lovely parallax'

[07:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of that church. But if you want to do a longer track, it\'s going to slowly, over time, end up at the side of your frame like this. Now, [snorts] you might want that to stay in the center. And that\'s where'

[07:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'deep track comes in. I\'m going to do this off camera because I can\'t do it whilst filming with my screen, unfortunately. It\'s deep tracked. And as I move, even though it\'s lost it, hopefully it will grab back it. There'

[07:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you go. It\'s grabbed it back on. Now, as I get right to the side of the frame, come all the way over here, and we still have the church mainly in the center of the frame.'

[07:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, that is how you shoot a parallax shot keeping your subject centered. I have one massive favor [music] to ask. If you enjoyed this video and the last, and you want to see more content like'

[07:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this, I really appreciate you subscribing to my channel. I put so much time and effort [music] into these and I\'m really trying to grow my following. So, any help I can get from you guys is so appreciated. Another popular topic of conversation'

[08:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'has been frame rates. What I used as my base frame rate for the first video and what I like to film when I\'m out and about doing travel vlogs. For travel and vlog style content, I always try to shoot at either 50 or 60 frames a second. I find it much'

[08:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] smoother on the eye for content with significant motion, street scenes, theme parks, etc. But, the main reason is it gives me [music] the option for half slow motion during the edit if I want to put clips together in a'

[08:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cinematic section [music] to music, kind of my signature. There are times, however, when I want significantly slower motion &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; for specific dramatic compositions and movement. For those, I will usually shoot a second clip at 120 [music] FPS,'

[08:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sometimes a slightly different angle. When I shoot at 60 or 120 FPS, I usually use a matching base timeline [music] of 60 frames per second. What are some of the things I loved about using the'

[08:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Luna Ultra? Now, I\'m going to hold my full review for a later date because there\'s still a lot I\'m learning, I\'m getting to grips with the camera, and I\'ve been shooting in Dolby Vision and the Pure Video night mode. Those are going to be in upcoming'

[09:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'videos for you. Here are a few things that I\'ve just handpicked that have stuck out to me that I really loved. Firstly, the detachable screen. It\'s a total game-changer. It allows for so much dynamic creativity in shots. You'

[09:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can film yourself really easily, but it\'s also great for filming subjects like animals and birds discreetly without disturbing them. When paired with Deep Track, makes it incredibly easy to film challenging angles,'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'especially whilst walking. It\'s a killer combination of features that produces gorgeous results. It kind of goes without saying, but the mechanical stabilization really is insane. And I know this because on the morning'

[09:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my Insta360 Ultra arrived, I decided to go and fracture my thumb in a car door. So, the entirety of my first film was shot with my non-dominant left hand. And the results speak for themselves. So, let\'s talk a little about telephoto'

[09:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lens. I really appreciate what Insta360 have done here and how they\'ve integrated the telephoto into the whole camera system. It\'s allowed for the color profiles, so standard color, film looks, I-Log, and Dolby Vision all to work consistently'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'across all focal ranges, 16 mm to 240. Now, this is something the main competition, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; you know who I\'m talking about, are not offering across both of their lenses. Higher frame rates of 100 and 120 FPS'

[10:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are available at native focal lengths of one times, which is 20 mm, and three times, which is 60 mm, offering more flexibility than my iPhone 17 Pro, which restricts slow motion of 120 frames per'

[10:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'second to the main lens only. I\'m also super impressed with the image quality at 120 mm or six times lossless [music] zoom. Now, this is a sensor crop, but it\'s a lossless crop, and it\'s'

[10:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'surprising how good this is. Now, some super important things, white balance, auto exposure, and focus. These are all excellent on the Insta360 Ultra. I shot 95% of my first film in full auto'

[11:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mode and was really impressed with how smooth the transitions [music] in exposure and white balance were between different conditions. This is likely due to the dedicated light sensor positioned between the lenses. Focus was'

[11:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'equally impressive. I hadn\'t found or needed the tap-to-focus mode. The camera\'s impressive AI processing always managed to get the focus spot-on. I didn\'t have a single unusable shot'

[11:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'when [music] editing. The onboard microphones are also very solid. Okay, so it\'s really noisy here. Ambulances, police cars. We\'re shooting here on the Luna Ultra internal microphone in Omni mode. So, that\'s the Omni pickup pattern. So, it'

[11:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'should be picking up sound all around me. The question is, can it isolate my voice even though there\'s lots of, you know, background sounds going on? I\'ll cover audio in much more detail in my upcoming content, as well as talking specifically'

[11:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about feature I love, the mic Pro. And incidentally, I\'m filming this whole video right now with the Luna Ultra at two times zoom, which is 40 mm equivalent, and it\'s a crop of the main camera sensor, but the quality'

[12:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is still amazing. So, you can see [music] the Luna Ultra really can be used in a studio setting. So, to summarize, across the board, the Insta360 Luna Ultra really is a grab-and-go powerhouse. Are there any'

[12:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'things I\'d like to see added to the Luna Ultra? Of course, and I\'ll go through my full comprehensive list in my main review. But, here are a couple of things that I really would love to see added. Firstly, exposure lock. Now, at the moment, if'

[12:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you want to do a tracking shot and you\'re going between two kind of very contrasty scenes, the only way to lock your exposure [music] is to go into the pro menu, open up the manual exposure tab, and then manually change the ISO'

[12:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and shutter speed to manual values. This is a bit time-consuming, especially if you only want to lock exposure for one single shot. I would love to see an exposure lock toggle similar to what you see on a mirrorless camera. And it\'d be really nice if we could add this to one'

[13:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of the custom buttons. Motion time lapse. This is something the competition does offer, and I feel like it\'s missing on the Luna Ultra here. Basically, it\'s a time lapse mode which allows the camera to slowly pan from left to right as it\'s creating the time lapse. It just'

[13:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] gives a bit more of a dynamic look to your time lapses. Lastly, a feature that\'s probably never going to come, but it\'s something that\'s on my wish list, and I call it Waypoint Motion. It would allow you to set a [music] start, middle, and end point'

[13:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with the joystick, assign a clip duration, and then hit a go button to have the camera create a smooth automatic motion track using the points entered. This really would be an amazing way to [music] capture skylines, street'

[13:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scenes, nature in a controlled and professional way. The applications for this are endless. In my Luna Ultra series, I\'ll be testing Dolby Vision and Pure Video Night Mode straight out of the camera just like my'

[13:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'last film. I\'ll also be exploring i-log and my color grading workflow just to see how much flexibility and quality you can squeeze out of the Luna Ultra. I\'ll bring it all together for a full review [music] covering image quality, audio,'

[14:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'usability, and everything else. Make sure you\'re subscribed [music] so you don\'t miss those videos and thanks again for all the support. I\'ll catch you all next time.'
